    # the rules commit, the counting.sh commit and the passthrough commit) and by
    # the paths they touch, no doc commit after a code commit, each commit
    # message's form and the count rule on every commit, the doc commit's three
    # files against the hashes planning's brief gave and against the hashes its
    # own message gives, each commit's diff hashed, each file's mode kept, the
    # rules commit's lines added only and only inside "Rules for every phase",
    # four bullets each signed by specs/0029, the counting.sh commit's one line
    # pair, no crate, tool, manifest or lock change, the gate file the phase
    # changed and the self-test it requires (its log naming a commit in the
    # range, its pass, no gate file after it, its phase line, its standard error
    # and its exit file), the scripts parsed and compiled, the new and modified
    # sources scored, the public fn and const first lines equal to the base's,
    # the consumer crate of part 6 P3 naming the call with the features off,
    # comments alone, copy alone and the two together, clippy and doc with the
    # features off, copy alone, comments alone, the two together and every
    # feature, clippy over the probe crate's feature sets, the crate's tests with
    # the features off, comments alone, copy alone, copy with comments and every
    # feature on both targets, no test file changed, the four DEBUG binary
    # hashes and their copies kept, this script's own stderr counted, and the
    # working tree's status, planning's uncommitted spec allowed.
    #
    # Usage: PRUNE_PREVIOUS=list|yes SELF_TEST_LOG=<the self-test's log> m3p7-p1-gate.sh
    # <phase commit> > <file outside the tree>; the caller moves the output to
    # records/logs/m3p7-p1/gate.log. The log prints its own
    # invocation, and every environment input it reads on a labelled line after it.
    #
    # This is a FILE, not an inline block, so "$0" names it and the log prints the
    # script rather than the shell binary.
    #
    # Its own text is committed inside the log, so it holds no office file name, no
    # path shape and no address: the office regex is read from check.sh, the
    # pre-P6d path forms are read from git, and every control fixture is assembled
    # at run time from pieces (specs/0001-bootstrap.md, as in every earlier gate log).
